  "lineage": "Minangkabau gong-chime music of West Sumatra played on small bronze kettle gongs (here the canang card). In talempong pacik several players each hold gongs in the hand and interlock their parts into a melody, while in talempong duduak the gongs lie in a row on a frame; both are usually joined by gandang drums and often a sarunai shawm, for weddings, processions and randai theatre.",
